<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above results was approved in the meeting of the Board of Directors held on 15th June, 2020.  n2. The company operates in a single operating segment of manufacturing of equipments. The results of the Company are also available on Stock Exchange websites and on the Companies website www.revathi.in.  n3. The Company has adopted Ind AS 116  Leases  effective from April 1, 2019 and applied the same to lease contracts existing on April 1, 2019 with right of use asset recognised to an amount equal to adjusted lease liability. Accordingly the comparatives for the year ended March 31, 2019 have not been retrospectively adjusted.  n4. The company has invested 25.20 crores in Semac Construction Technologies India LLP during the quarter.  n5. The company has further acquired 40916 shares of Semac Construction (P) Ltd for Rs.1.32 crores during the quarter.  n6. The company didn’t had any impact on Revenues or Expenses for FY20 since factory was operating for planned productions with required staff.  n7. The company faced following issues during nationwide lock-down for first quarter of FY21.  n      a. Delays in deliveries due to transportation.  n      b. Company could not able to get orders for Spares and Service.  n      c. Company faced weak collections.  n8. Previous year figures has been regrouped wherever considered necessary.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
